  "summary": "Six preprints posted in November 2026 present tools for species typing, 16S data conversion, genome alignment, and pathogen SNP analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the development of accessible computational workflows for microbial genomics and amplicon profiling, with emphasis on reproducibility, species-level resolution, and data interoperability. Robust Cluster Typing applies a ribosomal-protein-based genome workflow to species-level clustering, validated on Campylobacter. RADSuite addresses species-level identification in 16S microbiome studies through a curated rRNA gene copy database and V-region identification. VPHYL converts Emu and EPI2ME wf-16s nanopore abundance tables into phyloseq and BIOM objects with automated HTML reports. nf-core/pairgenomealign provides a Nextflow pipeline for scalable pairwise whole-genome alignment using LAST across evolutionary distances. SNP2Cluster-Py adds epidemiological and temporal context to core SNP distance clustering of pathogen genomes. Sparrowhawk contributes a WebAssembly route to private, in-browser interactive analysis. The new elements are mainly at the tool level, namely validated workflows and privacy-preserving deployment, rather than new biological findings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
